WEBVTT

00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:13,170
This is for my grand-babies again, here's grandpa's story, an army of ants.

00:00:13,170 --> 00:00:20,410
Our picnic was swell, Bob Sandwiches too, and grandma made jello that was red-white

00:00:20,410 --> 00:00:22,410
and blue.

00:00:22,410 --> 00:00:30,290
Aunt Edna brought coleslaw and bread from the oven, and her special recipe of poppy seed

00:00:30,290 --> 00:00:34,390
muffin.

00:00:34,390 --> 00:00:40,430
Pa spread the red checkerboard, blake it out straight, while I placed some rocks on the

00:00:40,430 --> 00:00:42,710
quarter for weight.

00:00:42,710 --> 00:00:46,670
Then Hilda, my sister, jumped down in the middle.

00:00:46,670 --> 00:00:54,980
About that same time, Uncle Bo grabbed his fiddle.

00:00:54,980 --> 00:00:59,820
He'd play a tune happy, so we'd want a dance.

00:00:59,820 --> 00:01:05,460
But it was right about then, and I spotted the ants.

00:01:05,460 --> 00:01:10,700
I was dumbfounded at first, didn't know what to say.

00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:17,480
A whole line of them carried one cupcake away.

00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:25,680
They were headed for Pa's special sauce chicken wings, who I tried to ward, but he started

00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:34,960
to sing, for the melody Uncle Bo strobed up so well was like magic that caught everyone

00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:38,220
in a spell.

00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:46,780
My horror was heightened, when I looked once more, I saw 10,000 ants take three pieces, no

00:01:46,780 --> 00:01:47,780
four.

00:01:47,780 --> 00:01:53,300
Oh, my, what was I, just a young boy to do?

00:01:53,300 --> 00:02:00,790
There's more ants than would fit in an entire zoo.

00:02:00,790 --> 00:02:05,230
They spotted my favorite cherry parfait.

00:02:05,230 --> 00:02:08,790
They're stealing pretty much half our buffet.

00:02:08,790 --> 00:02:11,830
The musk melon pretzels.

00:02:11,830 --> 00:02:23,340
The white chocolate mousse, my goodness, they've lifted the cooler of juice.

00:02:23,340 --> 00:02:27,260
There goes the cucumber salad, Bob, made.

00:02:27,260 --> 00:02:31,300
The strawberries didn't stand a chance, I'm afraid.

00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:42,980
The barbecue ribs disappeared in a flash, along with just about all of our bash.

00:02:42,980 --> 00:02:49,420
That was right about then that I got their attention, all one last thing that I think

00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:51,580
I should mention.

00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:58,580
When they carried away the last egg for the record, they came back and stole her blanket, all

00:02:58,580 --> 00:03:02,860
checkered.

00:03:02,860 --> 00:03:10,820
The siggy then stopped, and smiles faded to wonder, who can have caused all the pillage

00:03:10,820 --> 00:03:12,660
and plunder.

00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:15,220
But before I could speak.

00:03:15,220 --> 00:03:21,940
We all looked in surprise, for here came an invasion of thousands of flies.

